            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute the three points into ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "y=ax^2+bx+c",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and solve for the coefficients.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $y=ax^2+bx+c$. Using $(0,1)$ gives $c=1$.\n\nUsing $(2,3)$:\n$$4a+2b=2\\qquad (1)$$\nUsing $(4,13)$:\n$$16a+4b=12\\qquad (2)$$\nSubtract twice equation (1) from equation (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}(16a+4b)-2(4a+2b)&=12-2(2)\\\\8a&=8\\\\a&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $a=1$ into equation (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}4(1)+2b&=2\\\\2b&=-2\\\\b&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nThe equation is\n$$y=x^2-x+1.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
